  "falsified_or_bounded_models": [
    "Target-specific L11H2/L11H5 query transfer is effectively null in both splits; the pair is not licensed as a target-dependent Q gate.",
    "Corrupting the six earlier candidate heads has only a 0.056-0.059 logit effect, below the frozen 0.25 SESOI; their rescue through the late pair is not a qualified directed path.",
    "The eight attention heads are not a self-contained sparse circuit inside the declared CLS-write universe."
  ],
  "licensed_claim": "L11H2/L11H5 is a replicated, layer-specific two-head causal core of the fine-tuned promoter classifier's CLS readout: in both directions and both splits it exceeds every candidate-excluding two-head pair in layer 11. Strict complement scrub shows that the pair and full C8 set retain only about 14-15% alone but C8 plus all MLP writes retains about 61%, implicating a distributed MLP scaffold.",
  "mechanistic_model": "The supported model is a late L11H2/L11H5 output-carrier core operating on a representation maintained by distributed MLP writes, not a target-dependent query gate or a demonstrated early-six-to-late chain.",
  "next_gate": "Do not open source-band or motif surgery under v1. A new frozen assay must first justify direct K/V and source-state interventions for the replicated late pair without assuming the rejected early-to-late path.",
